    {
      "id": "claim_17336969115a4b90826859e4e681616a",
      "statement": "validateFileMetadata is the single size gate and enforces two bounds because metaData.size is peer-controlled: a size that is not finite or is <= 0 is rejected with 'invalid file size' (such a value would otherwise make the receiver flip the file to Success on a partial/empty payload or break the progress math), and size > maxSize (default 1 GB via DEFAULT_RECEIVE_OPTIONS) fails with a limit message; receiver-side validation failure sends EVENT_VALIDATE_ERROR back to the sender and records the error on the file, while autoAccept (default true) makes the receiver accept valid files without user action.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/receiver/Receiver.svelte#L80-L94",
