    {
      "id": "claim_e5da1d3058e24c759841da47ea4689bc",
      "statement": "onMetaData registers the file entry at WaitingAccept BEFORE the async AES key decryption, so the file is visible and removable throughout; if the RSA key unwrap fails, the entry gets a visible error, an error toast fires, and EVENT_VALIDATE_ERROR is sent to the sender (bouncing its file to Pending) instead of the file silently never appearing while the sender waits for an accept that will not come.",
      "evidence": [
