    {
      "id": "claim_11213eddf7234cdebeadcbe06e9cfeda",
      "statement": "The receiver 'Max Size' dropdown options carry true byte values matching their labels (10 MB = 10 * 1024 * 1024, 100 MB = 100 * 1024 * 1024, 'Unlimit' = 1 TiB); previously the 10/100 MB options were 1024x smaller than their labels and enforced KB limits (PR #44). onChange coerces the select value with Number(maxSize) and falls back to DEFAULT_RECEIVE_OPTIONS.maxSize when not finite, because bind:value on a <select> yields a string after user interaction, so ReceiveOptions.maxSize stays a number at runtime. tests/receiver-options-size.test.mjs statically pins these option values and the coercion.",
