    {
      "id": "claim_e5d9301a3cb54569b1dad0720e9bd1ff",
      "statement": "A chunk that fails AES-GCM authentication is rejected visibly, not dropped: processChunk routes the decrypt failure to rejectCorruptChunk, which marks the file errored ('corrupt data in transit'), bounces the status back to Pending, toasts the failure, sends EVENT_RECEIVER_REJECT so the sender stops cleanly, and tears down the per-file chunk/stats/queue state — instead of the byte count never catching up and the file sitting in Processing forever; the EVENT_RECEIVED_CHUNK ack is sent only after successful decryption so a corrupt chunk never advances the sender.",
      "evidence": [
