    {
      "id": "claim_41f3607445754c79a1129328ab10276e",
      "statement": "Removing a file while its chunk pipeline is in flight is safe: onRemove sets the stop flag (when Processing) before deleting the entry; the async pipeline only ever dereferences the entry reference captured at onSend entry (never a live re-read of sendingFiles[key] after an await), re-checks stop and the live entry at every await boundary, and the event handlers bail when the live entry is gone — so no continuation can dereference a deleted entry (previously an uncaught TypeError from sendingFiles[key].aesKey/.progress) or send a chunk into the void.",
